cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this project, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "finance-data-analysis-lab: descriptive financial analytics on real daily market data"
authors:
  - family-names: Monavvari
    given-names: Aydin
    email: 245710241+aydinmonavvari@users.noreply.github.com
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-08"
repository-code: "https://github.com/aydinmonavvari/finance-data-analysis-lab"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  An educational research project that applies descriptive quantitative analysis
  to raw daily financial market data. The repository transforms Yahoo Finance
  adjusted prices for seven US large-cap equities and the SPY benchmark into
  interpretable investment and risk information: log and simple returns,
  annualized return and volatility, Sharpe, Sortino and Calmar ratios, maximum
  drawdown, beta and alpha versus the benchmark, plus Jarque-Bera normality,
  Augmented Dickey-Fuller stationarity and Ljung-Box autocorrelation tests.
  The project is descriptive, not predictive, and provides no investment advice.
keywords:
  - quantitative finance
  - descriptive analytics
  - risk analysis
  - return statistics
  - drawdown
  - Sharpe ratio
  - normality tests
  - educational research
